            },
            {
              "id": "p6-q88-b-tower",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "L=\\sqrt{2}^{\\sqrt{2}^{\\sqrt{2}^{\\cdots}}}.",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p6-q88-b-show",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Show that ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "L^2=2^L",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$L^2=2^L$.\n\nThe repeated tower gives $L=(\\sqrt{2})^L$; square both sides and use the power-of-a-power law.",
          "worked": "Using the stated convergence and the repeated tower,\n$$L=(\\sqrt{2})^L.$$\nSquaring both sides,\n$$\\begin{align*}L^2&=\\left((\\sqrt{2})^L\\right)^2\\\\L^2&=(\\sqrt{2})^{2L}\\\\L^2&=2^L.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q88-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p6-q88-c-stem",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "By inspection, there are ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "two",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " possible solutions to the equation. Which is the correct value of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "L",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", and why is this the correct value?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$L=2$.\n\nThe positive candidates are $2$ and $4$. The sequence has $\\sqrt{2}\\le a_n<2$, so $\\sqrt{2}\\le L\\le2$, excluding $4$.",
          "worked": "The two positive candidates are $L=2$ and $L=4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2^2&=2^2\\\\4^2&=2^4.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a_1=\\sqrt{2}<2$, repeated use of part (a) gives $a_n<2$ for every $n$. Also $a_1=\\sqrt{2}>1$; whenever $a_n\\ge1$, the recurrence gives $a_{n+1}=(\\sqrt{2})^{a_n}\\ge\\sqrt{2}$. Hence every term is at least $\\sqrt{2}$.\nThe stated limit therefore satisfies\n$$\\sqrt{2}\\le L\\le2.$$\nOf the two positive candidates, only $L=2$ is possible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
    ]
